          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2473,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 850540490,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "So this for plugins? ([doc/README.tapping](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/doc/README.tapping))  \n```\nflags\nis a set of flags for the tap listener.  The flags that can be set are:\nSNIPPED\n    TL_REQUIRES_COLUMNS\n\n\tset if your tap listener \"packet\" routine requires the column\n\tstrings to be constructed.\nSNIPPED\n    If no flags are needed, use TL_REQUIRES_NOTHING.\n```\n  \ntshark is already doing it for taps:\n```\n        /* We only need the columns if either\n           1) some tap needs the columns\n           or\n           2) we're printing packet info but we're *not* verbose; in verbose\n           mode, we print the protocol tree, not the protocol summary.\n           */\n        if ((tap_flags & TL_REQUIRES_COLUMNS) || (print_packet_info && print_summary) || output_fields_has_cols(output_fields))\n            cinfo = &cf->cinfo;\n        else\n            cinfo = NULL;\n\n```\n  \nSince Lua says the columns are available read-only ([WSDG](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html/#lua_class_Pinfo)):\n```\n11.5.5.28. pinfo.columns\nMode: Retrieve only.\n\nAccess to the packet list columns.\n\n11.5.5.29. pinfo.cols\nMode: Retrieve only.\n```\n\nCould `tshark` check `wslua_count_plugins() > 0` then `need_columns=TRUE` ?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
